# Time Is Computed, Not Ticked

The only persisted time fields are:

- `startTimestamp` — server ms when the current run started
- `updated_at_ms` — server ms when the row last changed

`useTimer.tsx` recomputes `timeLeft` every **16ms** from:

```ts
const elapsedMs = (updatedAtMs - startTimestamp) + (now - updatedAtMs);
const positionInCycle = elapsedMs % cycleDurationMs; // prep + climb
```

The timer **auto-loops** — there is no "duration" field. Don't add one; derive
the current phase from `elapsed % cycleDurationMs`.

## Pause encoding

Pause is represented by `stopTimeMilliseconds != null` (frozen remaining time
in the current phase). Resume reconstructs a **new** `startTimestamp` such
that `now - startTimestamp` equals the elapsed-at-pause:

```ts
// Resume: shift startTimestamp forward by the paused duration
const newStart = getAdjustedNow() - elapsedAtPause;
```

Don't introduce a separate "isPaused" boolean — the presence/absence of
`stopTimeMilliseconds` is the single source of truth for pause state.
